<details class="performance-notes" id="periodic-time-rules"><summary>Provisional Time rules and data coverage</summary>
  <p>The user authorized these recommendations while awaiting Hadi. Periodic Tickets defines expectation and completion sets; this page does not redefine them. Current Ticket Owner controls ticket results. Personal time follows time_entries.user_id (the person booked to the entry), not its creator author_id or a substituted Ticket Owner.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>DTC = latest qualifying completion date minus creation date in calendar days; same-day closure is zero. It includes pauses and is not Start Date age or In Progress cycle time. Priority means current Urgent/Immediate, using existing mapping. Targets are separate optional global settings.</li>
    <li>Ticket cost compares current positive PM estimates with visible lifetime direct ticket hours through RED on the same available tickets. Earlier work is included; future work dates and child rollups are excluded. This differs from personal logged hours, which use only work dates within RSD–RED. Backdated records can change historical reruns.</li>
    <li>Expected Done owner-hours comparison uses the configured share % of those completed expected tickets' PM estimates. Both sides use matching estimate/time-available tickets. The reconciliation separately retains all known Expected Done hours, including hours on tickets without usable estimates.</li>
    <li>Personal total includes valid visible entries booked to the selected users on in-scope eligible tickets, even if another person currently owns the ticket. Classify against the logged user's own expectation package: completed expected, unfinished expected, other, or owner-unavailable review. Unlinked entries, excluded trackers/statuses/projects and invisible issues are outside this scope.</li>
    <li>Capacity = configured workdays × each owner's configured daily hours. Reuses current weekdays, holidays, default hours and optional visible weekly-hours mapping. Private/missing/invalid weekly values use the default without disclosure. Total deviation is Actual−Plan. Daily actual divides summed hours by summed owner-workdays; zero workdays is N/A.</li>
    <li>Other work has plan zero and raw P−A. A nonempty expectation fully completed with no debt at RED qualifies that owner's other hours as favorable Extra Work. This is an end-of-period classification, not proof the hours happened after the final expected completion. Team Extra and Unplanned hours remain separate; one owner's extra work does not erase another's shortfall. Raw P−A is kept in audit tables.</li>
    <li>CW/h uses a paired full expectation portfolio with usable current weights, PM estimates and owner-time visibility. Actual = delivered expected weight / logged-user hours on that portfolio, including unfinished work. Plan = expected portfolio weight / (share % × its PM estimate). Both sides exclude unsupported contributors with linked coverage. Zero effort is N/A. Deviation is Actual−Plan, superseding the Excel's conflicting P−A label provisionally.</li>
    <li>DTC and ticket-cost trends group the final RED Done population by completion interval. Personal-hour trends use entry work dates. CW/h combines delivered weight in the interval with portfolio hours worked in the interval; its plan is the full-portfolio rate reference. Coverage portfolios are fixed across intervals. Partial weeks/months are labelled; no future points or invented linear allocation.</li>
    <li>Positive deviation is favorable, negative unfavorable, zero neutral. Cost overrun within the existing estimate allowance is amber and beyond it red. Other metrics have no new tolerance. Missing targets, permission gaps and invalid time never become healthy zeros. Zero authorized visible entries means zero; negative/nonfinite/invalid time is flagged and excluded from comparisons.</li>
    <li>Team ticket costs and hours sum. DTC uses ticket-weighted durations; daily hours use summed owner-workdays; efficiency divides summed weights by summed effort. Owner averages and ratios are not averaged into team results. Current field/calendar/target edits can change past reports.</li>
  </ul>
</details>
